  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reconstruction and Localisation Efforts in Hromadas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The full-scale invasion of Ukraine continues to cause unprecedented levels of displacement, human suffering, and extensive damage to both private and public infrastructure. Its impacts are immediate in terms of humanitarian needs and massive in terms of long-term socioeconomic recovery, reconstruction, and prospects for peace and stability, with significant social, economic, and infrastructural disruption, testing the resilience of communities and institutions. To address the needs of targeted locations, IOM will implement a multi-tiered response that focuses on empowering local ownership of the recovery process; understanding and addressing barriers to durable solutions and broader recovery, inclusive of small-scale infrastructure rehabilitation.</narrative>
  </description>
